blocks.en:
Compared Methods. We compare our proposed method, HAS, against four frame sampling methods. These are:
(1) UNI, which samples frames at fixed temporal intervals across the video’s timeline and serves as the default method for the models evaluated in this paper;
(2) TOP, which selects frames in descending order of their query-relevance scores;
(3) AKS [ 25 ] , an enhancement of TOP that simultaneously considers both the relevance of a frame and the temporal coverage of the already selected set of frames and (4) TSTAR [ 31 ] , which select question-relevant frames via object-centric visual search rather than semantic similarity, iteratively narrowing down the temporal region of interest through coarse-to-fine resampling.

blocks.zh:
比较方法。 我们把拟议方法与四个框架取样方法进行比较。 它们是:
(1) UNI -- -- 在整个录像时间范围内按固定时间间隔取样,并作为本文所评价的模型的默认方法;
(2) TOP,按其查询相关分数的下行顺序选择帧;
(3)AKS [25],即对TOP的增强,既考虑一个帧的相关性,又考虑已经选定的一组帧的时间覆盖范围;和(4)TSTAR [31],即通过以物体为中心的视觉搜索,而不是语义上的相似性,选择出与问题相关的帧,通过粗对细的再生来迭接地缩小感兴趣的时区.
